{
  "level": "Year 8",
  "subject": "maths",
  "title": "Like terms and simplifying",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "Notes and coins",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A till has 20 dollar notes and 2 dollar coins.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 290,
            "alt": "$20 notes and $2 coins counted in separate piles, like x² and x terms",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 50,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "$20"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 150,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "$20"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 330,
                "y": 90,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 430,
                "y": 90,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 380,
                "y": 190,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "You count the notes together, and the coins together.",
          "write": "separate piles"
        },
        {
          "say": "x squared and x are like notes and coins. Different kinds of term.",
          "write": "x² and x: different",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 290,
            "alt": "$20 notes and $2 coins counted in separate piles, like x² and x terms",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 50,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "$20"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 150,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "$20"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 330,
                "y": 90,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 430,
                "y": 90,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 380,
                "y": 190,
                "r": 40,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "$2"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 110,
                "y": 270,
                "text": "x²",
                "size": 26,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 380,
                "y": 270,
                "text": "x",
                "size": 26,
                "color": "orange",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So 5 x squared plus 3x stays just as it is.",
          "write": "5x² + 3x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "What makes like terms?",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Like terms have the same letters, with the same powers.",
          "write": "same letters, same powers"
        },
        {
          "say": "4 x squared y and minus 3 y x squared are like terms.",
          "write": "4x²y and −3yx²  ✓"
        },
        {
          "say": "Order doesn't matter. Both are x times x times y.",
          "write": "yx² = x²y"
        },
        {
          "say": "x squared y and x y squared are not. The square is on a different letter.",
          "write": "x²y and xy²  ✗"
        },
        {
          "say": "7 a squared and 7a are not like terms either. Different powers.",
          "write": "7a² and 7a  ✗"
        },
        {
          "say": "Tip. Put the letters in alphabetical order. Then like terms look identical.",
          "write": "yx² → x²y"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Collecting like terms",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Simplify 7 p squared, minus 3p, plus 2 p squared, plus 8p.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "alt": "Terms 7p², −3p, 2p² and 8p sorted into a p² pile and a p pile",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "7p²"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 160,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "−3p"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 290,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "2p²"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "8p"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "7p² − 3p + 2p² + 8p",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Each term keeps its sign. Sort them into piles.",
          "write": "sort by type",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "alt": "Terms 7p², −3p, 2p² and 8p sorted into a p² pile and a p pile",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "7p²",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 160,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "2p²",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 300,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "−3p"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 110,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "8p"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 155,
                "y": 150,
                "text": "p² pile",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "blue",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 415,
                "y": 150,
                "text": "p pile",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "orange",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "7p² − 3p + 2p² + 8p",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "7 plus 2 is 9. Minus 3 plus 8 is 5.",
          "write": "= 9p² + 5p",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "alt": "Terms 7p², −3p, 2p² and 8p sorted into a p² pile and a p pile",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 95,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 120,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "9p²",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 355,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 120,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "5p",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 155,
                "y": 150,
                "text": "7 + 2 = 9",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "blue",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 415,
                "y": 150,
                "text": "−3 + 8 = 5",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "orange",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "= 9p² + 5p",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Only the numbers change. The power stays the same.",
          "write": "3x² + 2x² = 5x²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Write the highest power first. That's descending order.",
          "write": "9p² + 5p − 4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Negative coefficients",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Use your integer rules on the coefficients.",
          "write": "−3a² + 5a² = 2a²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Minus 4m, minus 6m. Start at minus 4, go down 6. Minus 10m.",
          "write": "−4m − 6m = −10m"
        },
        {
          "say": "Minus 5a minus 2a is minus 7a. Not minus 3a.",
          "write": "−5a − 2a = −7a"
        },
        {
          "say": "A constant like plus 4 has no partner. It just stays.",
          "write": "−7a − 4b + 4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Times first, then tidy",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Same order of operations as numbers. Multiply and divide first.",
          "write": "× ÷ before + −"
        },
        {
          "say": "2a times 3b is 6ab. Then add 5ab.",
          "write": "2a × 3b + 5ab"
        },
        {
          "say": "6ab plus 5ab is 11ab.",
          "write": "= 6ab + 5ab = 11ab"
        },
        {
          "say": "12 x squared divided by 4x is 3x. Then take away x.",
          "write": "12x² ÷ 4x − x = 3x − x"
        },
        {
          "say": "That leaves 2x.",
          "write": "= 2x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Perimeter of a rectangle",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A rectangle is 3x plus 2y long and x minus y wide.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/like-terms-and-simplifying-ex5.svg",
          "alt": "A rectangle with lengths (3x + 2y) cm and widths (x − y) cm"
        },
        {
          "say": "Add all four sides. The x terms make 8x.",
          "write": "3x + x + 3x + x = 8x"
        },
        {
          "say": "The y terms make 2y. So the perimeter is 8x plus 2y.",
          "write": "P = 8x + 2y cm"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check with x equals 5 and y equals 2. Both give 44.",
          "write": "19 + 3 + 19 + 3 = 44 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Adding doesn't change the power. Not 5 x to the 4.",
          "write": "✗ 3x² + 2x² = 5x⁴"
        },
        {
          "say": "x squared y and x y squared don't combine.",
          "write": "x²y ≠ xy²"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't add before you multiply.",
          "write": "× first, then +"
        },
        {
          "say": "Circle each term with its sign, so you don't lose a minus.",
          "write": "−5a − 2a = −7a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
